WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.606
Access reviews are recurring attestation

2
00:00:02.606 --> 00:00:05.162
that each person still
needs what they hold.

3
00:00:05.162 --> 00:00:08.810
Each instance captures a snapshot
of access when it starts,

4
00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:12.012
and changes during a review
show up in the next cycle.

5
00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:14.000
The schedule is set by risk.

6
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.180
Privileged roles are reviewed in PIM,
monthly for Tier 0 by the Tier 0 approver

7
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:24.037
group, and quarterly for the other
tiers, with removal if nobody responds.

8
00:00:24.037 --> 00:00:28.800
Tier 1 application groups are reviewed
quarterly in two stages of seven days:

9
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.851
the manager first, then
the application owner for

10
00:00:31.851 --> 00:00:34.976
everyone the manager approved
or marked don't know.

11
00:00:34.976 --> 00:00:37.962
That replaces the old
manual escalation step.

12
00:00:37.962 --> 00:00:41.280
Tier 2 groups are semiannual
and Tier 3 annual,

13
00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:44.162
by the application or department owner.

14
00:00:44.162 --> 00:00:47.084
Guests are reviewed
quarterly by their sponsors,

15
00:00:47.084 --> 00:00:49.863
and denied guests are
blocked and then removed.

16
00:00:49.863 --> 00:00:51.662
Four rules make reviews bite.

17
00:00:51.662 --> 00:00:55.025
First, review the groups,
not the applications.

18
00:00:55.025 --> 00:00:59.586
Microsoft notes that reviewing an application
that uses group assignment doesn't

19
00:00:59.586 --> 00:01:03.750
remove the members of those groups; they
keep their access through the group.

20
00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:07.514
Second, whenever reviewers
are managers or group owners,

21
00:01:07.514 --> 00:01:12.400
add a fallback reviewer for users with
no manager and groups with no owner.

22
00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.850
Third, choose the no-response
default deliberately.

23
00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:19.889
Microsoft warns that combining
remove access with auto-apply

24
00:01:19.889 --> 00:01:23.850
can revoke all access to a resource
if reviewers don't respond.

25
00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:28.737
So the program sets remove only where an
unreviewed grant is riskier than a lost

26
00:01:28.737 --> 00:01:32.588
one, privileged roles and guests,
and no change with escalation

27
00:01:32.588 --> 00:01:36.512
for business applications, where
a mass removal would stop work.

28
00:01:36.512 --> 00:01:39.333
Fourth, justification on every decision,

29
00:01:39.333 --> 00:01:42.401
and no bulk decisions
on privileged reviews.

30
00:01:42.401 --> 00:01:46.124
The service can't prevent a bulk
action, so the history is checked

31
00:01:46.124 --> 00:01:50.200
for one reviewer recording many
identical decisions within minutes.

32
00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:54.746
The records: results download as a
CSV, and review history reports stay

33
00:01:54.746 --> 00:02:00.140
downloadable for only thirty days, so each
one goes straight to the evidence store.
